Core concepts
Dataset: collection of related information (employees, sales, applicants, customers, products, website activity, surveys).
DataFrame: main Pandas object; a table of rows and columns; programmable spreadsheet.
Series: one column of a DataFrame.
Rows: one record each. Columns: one type of information each.
Index: labels that identify rows (default starts at zero). Use for locating rows, resetting after filter, or meaningful IDs.
Data types: int, float, object/string, bool, datetime. Wrong types break calculations, dates as text, numbers as text, odd filters.
Check with df.dtypes and df.info().

Loading and viewing
import pandas as pd
Common sources: CSV, Excel, JSON, database queries, APIs.
df = pd.read_csv("employees.csv")
df = pd.read_excel("employees.xlsx")
Viewing: df.head(), df.tail(), df.sample()
Structure: df.shape, df.columns, df.info(), df.describe(), df.isna().sum()

Selecting data
Columns: df["salary"] or df[["name", "salary"]]
loc: label based rows and columns, often with filters and edits
iloc: position based rows and columns
Filter: df[df["salary"] > 50000]
Multiple: & | ~ with parentheses around each condition
isin: df[df["city"].isin(["Kathmandu", "Lalitpur"])]
Text: df[df["name"].str.contains("a", case=False, na=False)]
Sort: df.sort_values("salary", ascending=False); multi column sort too
Top bottom: df.nlargest(3, "salary"), df.nsmallest(...)

Add edit delete
New column: from fixed value, existing columns, condition, calculation, transformation
df["annual_salary"] = df["salary"] * 12
Conditional: np.where for Senior/Junior style labels
Edit: df.loc[df["name"] == "Asha", "salary"] = 40000
Replace: df["city"] = df["city"].replace({"KTM": "Kathmandu", "LTP": "Lalitpur"})
Rename: df.rename(columns={...})
Drop columns: df.drop(columns=["rating"])
Drop rows: keep valid with filter, e.g. df[df["salary"] >= 20000]

Transform
Column math: df["bonus"] = df["salary"] * 0.10
apply: custom function on a column
map: dictionary lookup for category codes to labels

Missing values
isna/sum first. Drop with dropna(subset=...) when field is essential and few rows.
Fill: median for skewed numeric, mean when balanced, mode for categories, Unknown for text.
Mean vs median vs mode: choose based on distribution and column type.

Duplicates
duplicated(), drop_duplicates(), subset= and keep=

Text cleaning
strip and title for cities; case methods; split email into username and domain

Dates
pd.to_datetime(..., errors="coerce")
Extract: .dt.year, .dt.month, weekday
Filter by date range

Grouping and aggregation
Aggregations: count, sum, mean, median, min, max
groupby then agg with named outputs
value_counts and normalize=True for percentages

Combining
concat for stacking similar files
merge on shared key: inner, left, right, outer

Reshape
pivot_table for summary grids
melt for wide to long

Basic EDA
shape, dtypes, missing, duplicates, describe, unique/nunique, unusual values, corr
Correlation is not causation

Export
to_csv / to_excel with index=False
ExcelWriter for multiple sheets

Common mistakes
Wrong column name case; numbers/dates as text; missing parentheses in filters;
using and/or instead of &/|; accidentally changing original df; merge multiplying rows

Practical workflow
Load, preview, inspect, check quality, fix column names, fix types,
clean missing and duplicates, filter and transform, group or summarize, export

Good AI instructions
Name input, columns, filters, missing rules, duplicate rules, calculations,
grouping, sort, output columns, export format, whether original stays unchanged

